  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>thalidomide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L04AX02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Chen TL et al. 1989</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy male volunteers</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>thalidomide</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_thalidomide/Thalidomide_Chen1989_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>apparent volume of distribution</td><td>120.69</td><td>liters</td><td><small>V/F</small></td></tr><tr><td>total body clearance rate</td><td>10.41</td><td>liters/hr</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>urinary excretion of thalidomide</td><td>0.6</td><td>% of the total dose administered over 24 hr</td><td><small>fe</small></td></tr><tr><td>renal clearance rate</td><td>0.08</td><td>liter/hr</td><td><small>CLR</small></td></tr><tr><td>K a (1/h)</td><td>0.4</td><td>1/h</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr><tr><td>T lag (h)</td><td>0.73</td><td>h</td><td><small>tlag</small></td></tr></table><h4>About thalidomide</h4><p>Thalidomide is an immunomodulatory drug used for conditions such as multiple myeloma and leprosy, among several other immune and blood disorders. It remains authorised in the European Union for multiple myeloma, but its use is tightly controlled because it causes severe birth defects, and it was famously withdrawn from use as a sedative for this reason.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q203174\">Wikidata Q203174</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Thalidomide\">Thalidomide</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Chen TL et al. (1989). Plasma pharmacokinetics and urinary excretion of thalidomide after oral dosing in healthy male volunteers. <i>Drug metabolism and disposition: the biological fate of chemicals 17(4):402–405</i>. PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2571480\">2571480</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Chen_1989: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
